{"id": "section-body-12452", "title": "Neonatal Conjunctivitis (Ophthalmia Neonatorum)", "chapterId": "chapter-twelve", "blocks": [{"id": "body-12452", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Neonatal Conjunctivitis (Ophthalmia Neonatorum)", "runs": [{"text": "Neonatal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Conjunctivitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(Ophthalmia"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Neonatorum)"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1397"}}, {"id": "body-12453", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Ophthalmia Neonatorum (ON) means inflammation of the conjunctiva of a newborn baby of less than 1 month of age.", "runs": [{"text": "Ophthalmia"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Neonatorum"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(ON)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "means"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inflammation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "conjunctiva"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "newborn"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "baby"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "less"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "than"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "1"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "month"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "age."}]}, {"id": "body-12454", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Is a potentially sight threatening condition. If the baby is older, the cause is unlikely to be an STI. The main Causative agents include Neisseria gonorrhoeae and Chlamydia trachomatis. Other non-STI causes of neonatal conjunctivitis include Staphylococcus aureus, Streptococcus pneumoniae, Haemophilus and Pseudomonas spp, Viral, chemical and physical irritation.", "runs": [{"text": "Is a potentially sight threatening condition. If the baby is older, the cause is unlikely to be an STI."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "The main Causative agents include "}, {"text": "Neisseria gonorrhoeae ", "italic": true}, {"text": "and "}, {"text": "Chl